// Certificate and cache storage auth keeps on behalf of every node's ACME
// manager (services/auth/api_acme.go, services/auth/acme/store — the
// autocert.Cache implementation that turns these calls into Go's
// golang.org/x/crypto/acme/autocert.Cache interface for a caller elsewhere in
// the cloud). Two certificate stores exist side by side and neither maps onto
// the other: an ACME-issued certificate keyed by fqdn (Get/SetCertificate,
// backed by `/acme/...`) and an operator-injected one, also keyed by fqdn but
// with its own wildcard-domain fallback on read (Get/SetStaticCertificate,
// backed by `/static/...`, and clients/p2p/auth/certificates.go's
// InjectStaticCertificate). GetCache/SetCache/DeleteCache are the third
// store: autocert's own generic cache, keyed by an opaque name that is
// sometimes a certificate and sometimes an ACME challenge token, which is why
// it alone has a delete — autocert deletes challenge tokens once an order
